# Line endings.
#
# Everything tracked in this repo is text. Git stores it with LF; each working
# copy gets whatever its platform uses -- CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux/macOS.
# `text=auto` makes that automatic, so it no longer depends on a per-machine
# core.autocrlf setting being right. Without it, a tool reading the folder with
# autocrlf unset (a Linux checkout, WSL, a container, an agent) commits the
# Windows bytes verbatim and rewrites every line of the file -- which is what
# happened to HANDOFF.md in 9d1c70a.
#
# The repo was already LF-normalised when this was added, so it required no
# renormalise commit and no file content changed.

* text=auto

# --- Explicit, so intent survives a bad auto-detection ---

# Firmware sources and build inputs
*.c          text
*.h          text
*.s          text
*.ld         text

# STM32CubeMX configuration. Both are regenerated by CubeMX on whichever
# machine runs it; normalising them keeps a regeneration diff readable
# instead of a whole-file rewrite.
*.ioc        text
.mxproject   text

# Docs and repo metadata
*.md         text
*.txt        text
.gitignore   text
.gitattributes text

# --- Files that must keep specific endings regardless of platform ---
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bat        text eol=crlf
*.cmd        text eol=crlf

# --- Binaries: never touch, never diff as text ---
*.pdf        binary
*.png        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.gif        binary
*.ico        binary
*.elf        binary
*.bin        binary
*.hex        binary
*.a          binary
*.o          binary
